                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2b565b22-9fee-4b0c-a258-bb396839e36b",
                        "source_entry_id": "73215858-f931-33e6-ad92-7df508b4ee4c",
                        "source_sense_id": "3012f326-8c06-3c0f-bb28-da52ebeaa0f5",
                        "target_lang_word": "Beijing",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Beijing",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74036a4a-5c57-346c-b58a-bd0fed49a21e",
                                        "entry_id": "68d9ba8f-8c50-340c-bf41-67afd4487885",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A direct-administered municipality, the capital city of China."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e48a6696-3413-4540-8a08-02dc6beef8c4",
                                                "sense_id": "74036a4a-5c57-346c-b58a-bd0fed49a21e",
                                                "text": "Liu Lao-zheng sidled right up to Zao-hua and said: “That’s right. I went to Beijing [Peking] to visit with my daughter. Zao-hua, I hear that you have become the workpoint recorder.”[…]\nLiu Lao-zheng pulled out an abacus from a sack he was carrying over his shoulder. “Huala, huala,” he shook it several times and said: “I bought one in Beijing. I’ll lend it to you to use.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9de86817-5480-41a9-a530-96872caddb99",
                                                "sense_id": "74036a4a-5c57-346c-b58a-bd0fed49a21e",
                                                "text": "Backhoes moved house by house, laying waste to a community called Xitai that was built in a plush green valley on the northern edge of Beijing, only a short walk from the Great Wall of China."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94cc5afe-9274-4107-a425-c15fe550aaa1",
                                                "sense_id": "74036a4a-5c57-346c-b58a-bd0fed49a21e",
                                                "text": "A protester unfurled two banners on a highway overpass in central Beijing on Oct. 13, denouncing Xi Jinping as a “despotic traitor.” China’s censors went to great lengths to scrub the internet of any reference to the act of dissent, prohibiting all discussion and shutting down many offending social media accounts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "adfa4732-c846-40cb-a5bc-6f52c13ebbab",
                                                "sense_id": "74036a4a-5c57-346c-b58a-bd0fed49a21e",
                                                "text": "Beijing regularly faces dust storms in March and April due to its proximity to the Gobi desert as well as deforestation throughout northern China."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "966b479c-60fa-3ba1-afc1-5308b935866e",
                                        "entry_id": "68d9ba8f-8c50-340c-bf41-67afd4487885",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The government of the People's Republic of China."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "metonymically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf627714-fe92-4c78-9c06-75f2a7b21f9a",
                                                "sense_id": "966b479c-60fa-3ba1-afc1-5308b935866e",
                                                "text": "In Beijing’s view, in the absence of an explicit treaty provision, the central line of the main channel—the Thalweg principle—provided a legal basis for delimiting the boundary in the two rivers. On this basis, Beijing claimed that 600 of the rivers’ 700 islands—including Zhenbao Island on the Ussuri River, just 180 miles southwest of an important Soviet city, Khabarovsk—belonged to the P.R.C."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4264e3f-ac17-4c7b-b928-98a22cd858f7",
                                                "sense_id": "966b479c-60fa-3ba1-afc1-5308b935866e",
                                                "text": "In the Shanghai Communiqué of 1972, we recognized the fact that both Beijing and Taipei viewed Taiwan as part of China but unequivocally expressed our support for a peaceful settlement of the unification issue. While we should not alter the fundamental pillars of our policy, we should consider certain steps that will raise Taiwan's international standing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bce72b79-5eac-454c-a100-6406162fadf0",
                                                "sense_id": "966b479c-60fa-3ba1-afc1-5308b935866e",
                                                "text": "Russian officials have raised increasingly frustrated requests for greater support during discussions with Beijing in recent weeks, calling on China to live up to its affirmation of a “no limits” partnership made weeks before the war in Ukraine began. But China’s leadership wants to expand assistance for Russia without running afoul of Western sanctions and has set limits on what it will do, according to Chinese and U.S. officials."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "931e28bc-28b7-440b-9764-a594eaa3d0d4",
                                                "sense_id": "966b479c-60fa-3ba1-afc1-5308b935866e",
                                                "text": "While Beijing has credited the law with restoring peace and order to the city, it has been criticised by rights groups and western governments for imprisoning pro-democracy activists and undermining civil freedoms."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b74e1bb9-fdad-417c-8d8e-63571655899f",
                        "source_entry_id": "73215858-f931-33e6-ad92-7df508b4ee4c",
                        "source_sense_id": "3012f326-8c06-3c0f-bb28-da52ebeaa0f5",
